---
import SiteLayout from "../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { buildSeo, languageLink } from "../../../lib/pages";

// From the app repository's PRIVACY.md (last updated 2026-10-24, version 8.0).
const path = "/paper-sudoku/privacy/";
const alternatePath = "/zh/paper-sudoku/privacy/";
const seo = buildSeo({
  title: "Paper Sudoku Privacy Policy - Titpea",
  description:
    "How Paper Sudoku keeps your games on your device: no network permission, no account, no ads or analytics.",
  path,
  alternatePath,
  locale: "en",
  ogImage: "/assets/og-paper-sudoku.png",
});
---

<SiteLayout seo={seo} current="paper-sudoku" locale="en" language={languageLink("en", alternatePath)}>
  <article class="privacy-page shell">
    <header class="privacy-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        <a href="/paper-sudoku/">Paper Sudoku</a>
      </p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: October 24, 2026 (version 8.0)</p>
      <p class="lead">
        Paper Sudoku is an offline puzzle game. It does not require an account, does not contain ads or analytics, and
        does not request the <code>INTERNET</code> permission.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="privacy-content prose">
      <section>
        <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
        <p>The app stores only the data needed to run the game locally:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            your games (board, notes, undo history, the digits written in order, time, how much the Coach helped),
            including puzzles you type in, in a local Room database;
          </li>
          <li>finished-puzzle results (mode, difficulty, time, Coach use, date) for the notebook;</li>
          <li>
            settings (theme, note tidying, techniques you have met, and per technique how many pages you wrote with it
            yourself and when, whether you have written your first digit) in Android DataStore.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>The home-screen widget reads today's page from the same local database.</p>
        <p>
          The app has no network access and no server, analytics SDK, advertising SDK, or third-party tracking. If you
          use Android's own backup or device-to-device transfer, the system may include the database and settings above
          in your backup, under your Google account and Android's backup encryption; the developer cannot access it. You
          can turn this off in Android settings.
        </p>
        <p>
          Sharing a result sends only the text you see in the share sheet to the app you choose. Printing uses Android's
          print service and the printer or “Save as PDF” target you pick.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Permissions and sharing</h2>
        <p>
          The app does not request network, location, contacts, camera, microphone, notification or advertising
          permissions. It asks Android for exactly one, added by AndroidX:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <code>
              com.titpea.papersudoku.
              <wbr />
              DYNAMIC_RECEIVER_
              <wbr />
              NOT_EXPORTED_
              <wbr />
              PERMISSION
            </code>
            : a permission the app defines for itself (androidx.core adds it) so that only the app can message its own
            internal receivers.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>The widget's redraw just after midnight is an ordinary alarm and needs no permission.</p>
        <p>
          It gives access to no data. The app does not run foreground services. A build check fails if the app ever asks
          for anything else. The app does not share data with third parties.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>The app does not knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including children.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If a future version adds a feature that changes this policy, the policy and the Play Store Data Safety
          declaration will be updated before that version is published.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions, email <a href="mailto:info@titpea.com">info@titpea.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
